-- #151 방문 기반 관측 지표의 방문 기록 (ADR-0170; owner answers 151-1…151-5, ADR-0167 결정 6 and
-- 결정 8의 7·8). Generated by `drizzle-kit generate`, then hand-edited where marked: this header and
-- the tail. The snapshot is as generated. Additive: two new tables, their guards and one marker
-- row; no existing row changes, so no reset (docs/RESET.md).
--
-- - market_visits: one row per account, public market and Korean date on which a signed-in,
--   onboarded person not admin by the records opened that market's detail (151-3, 95-4) — the
--   account, the market and the date, nothing else (no time, address, device or referrer). The
--   date is the column default, the database clock's Korean date (ADR-0063): buddha_app may
--   INSERT only `user_id` and `market_id` (the tail's column grant), so no app write carries a
--   date. Its primary key merges a day's repeats; both FKs are RESTRICT like market_watch_events'
--   (a closure deletes no visit, 151-5); an index on the date serves the retention's batches.
-- - market_visit_collection: when the visit records began to be kept (ADR-0167 결정 8의 7 "#151
--   배포 전의 주"), one row at most, written below at the instant this migration is applied —
--   drizzle's journal keeps the authoring time, not this one. A provenance marker, not an
--   aggregate (95-8): no personal data, no count.
-- - retention_purges_kind_check: the purge records take the new kind `market_visits` (#184's
--   RETENTION_PURGE_KINDS, ADR-0167 결정 8의 8) — the generated drop and add of the CHECK, the list
--   as before (0078's) with the kind last, where a run takes it.
-- - No enum, event type, admin action type or release setting value: `retention.market_visits` is
--   registered in @buddha/shared with no value (undecided — 151-5), and nothing is deleted until
--   the owner approves one (ADR-0069 decision 7).
CREATE TABLE "market_visit_collection" (
	"id" boolean PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT true NOT NULL,
	"started_at" timestamp (3) with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "market_visit_collection_id_check" CHECK ("market_visit_collection"."id")
);
--> statement-breakpoint
CREATE TABLE "market_visits" (
	"user_id" text NOT NULL,
	"market_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"visit_date" date DEFAULT ((now() AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Seoul')::date) NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "market_visits_user_id_market_id_visit_date_pk" PRIMARY KEY("user_id","market_id","visit_date")
);
--> statement-breakpoint
